{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_adr", "label": "ADR 0001: two transport kinds instead of one interface", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Status accepted. Splits the transport contract by what a backend actually provides, because every intended backend (GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, Azure DevOps, OneDrive, SharePoint, filesystem, S3, Dropbox) is an object store with no delivery semantics."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_transport_interface", "label": "Original single Transport interface (connect/send/receive/health/close)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "lines 9-17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The design sketch's uniform interface. Rejected because send/receive asks each adapter to invent messaging on top of storage."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_reinvented_delivery_problem", "label": "Reinvented delivery semantics per adapter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "lines 24-31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Implementing receive against a store forces polling with adaptive backoff, acknowledgement, deduplication, redelivery with jitter, dead-lettering and chunking for the 100 MB blob limit, rewritten by every adapter author. Consequences: adapters become several hundred lines so fewer get written, each carries its own delivery bugs in a package this repo does not control, and the cost of entry undermines the open plugin ecosystem goal."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_store_kind", "label": "capabilities.kind === 'store'", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "put / get / list / delete, optional watch. Four methods is the whole adapter surface, which keeps the conformance suite strict and adapters small."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_native_kind", "label": "capabilities.kind === 'native'", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 39", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "send / subscribe. Kept for backends that genuinely are message systems, where synthesising acknowledgements on top of them would be wrong."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "label": "Mailbox engine in @fyrlabs/dead-drop/core", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Implements messaging once over the store primitives so delivery correctness is implemented once, tested once and fixed once. Cost: the runtime does more work, so its bugs affect every transport, mitigated by it being the most heavily tested code in the repository."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_delete_as_acknowledgement", "label": "Delete-as-acknowledgement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Acknowledgement is modelled as deleting the object, which is the only primitive a store offers; the side effect is that no record of a finished job survives."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_chunking_and_reassembly", "label": "Chunking and reassembly", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "lines 25, 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Needed because stores impose blob size limits such as GitHub's 100 MB; done once in the engine rather than per adapter."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_redelivery_with_backoff", "label": "Redelivery with backoff", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Automatic redelivery lives in the engine, which is why request-level retry is not exposed as a user-facing control."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_dead_letters", "label": "Dead letters", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Terminal destination for messages that exhaust redelivery, implemented once in the engine."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_deduplication", "label": "Deduplication", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Store-backed delivery is at-least-once, so the engine dedupes rather than each adapter."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_broadcast_topics_resume_cursor", "label": "Broadcast topics with a resume cursor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fan-out reads cannot use delete-as-acknowledgement, so subscribers track position with a cursor instead."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_adaptive_polling", "label": "Adaptive polling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "lines 25, 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stores have no push, and only optional watch, so the engine polls with adaptive backoff instead of requiring adapters to."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_conformance_suite", "label": "Transport conformance suite", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Can be strict precisely because the adapter surface is four methods."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_storebackedtransport", "label": "StoreBackedTransport base class (rejected alternative)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keep the single interface and ship a base class adapters extend. Rejected because inheritance across a package boundary is a versioning trap, and because it leaves the door open to adapters that half-implement delivery."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_plugin_ecosystem_goal", "label": "Open plugin ecosystem goal", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The force driving the split: a several-hundred-line cost of entry per adapter undermines third-party transports, so the contract has to be small enough that a store adapter is four methods."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_object_store_backends", "label": "Intended backends are all object stores", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "lines 19-21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, Azure DevOps, OneDrive, SharePoint, local filesystem, S3-compatible storage and Dropbox are every one an object store with no delivery semantics, which is the observation the whole ADR turns on."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_filesystem_transport", "label": "Filesystem transport (~300 lines, atomic writes, polling watcher)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cited as evidence the split works: a complete store adapter fits in about 300 lines including atomic writes and a polling watcher."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_transport_interface", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "lines 7-17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_reinvented_delivery_problem", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_transport_interface", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 25", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_object_store_backends", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_adr", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "lines 19-21", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_plugin_ecosystem_goal", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_adr", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_store_kind", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 38", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_native_kind", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 39", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_store_kind", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_delete_as_acknowledgement", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_chunking_and_reassembly", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_redelivery_with_backoff", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_dead_letters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_deduplication", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_broadcast_topics_resume_cursor", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_adaptive_polling", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_native_kind", "target": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_transports_mailbox_engine", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-store-and-native-transports.md", "source_location": "line 44", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_store_and_native_